<title>USA: Rykoff-Sexton Inc Q1 Sept 28 profit.</title>
<headline>Rykoff-Sexton Inc Q1 Sept 28 profit.</headline>
<dateline>LISLE, Ill. 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>				    Sep 28, 1996	  Oct 28, 1995</p>
<p> Net sales			    $904,827		 $440,545</p>
<p>Warehouse, selling, general and</p>
<p>  administrative expenses	  155,928		   91,627</p>
<p>Amortization of goodwill and</p>
<p>  other intangibles		    2,933			165</p>
<p> Income from operations	     18,526		    9,008</p>
<p>Interest and other expenses,</p>
<p>  net of interest income	    14,409		    4,213</p>
<p> Net income				2,046		    2,877</p>
<p> Earnings per share		     0.07		     0.19</p>
<p> Weighted avg shares outstanding  28,051		   15,068</p>
<p>NOTE: Year-ago results not directly comparable due to fiscal year change and US Foodservice merger on May 17, 1996.</p>
<p>Year-ago results include reclassification of certain operating expenses as cost of sales. Year-ago warehouse, selling, general and administrative expenses include $6.4 million reversal of restructuring reserve.</p>
<p>Earnings per share excluding amortization of goodwill would have been $0.16 for curent period and $0.19 a year ago.</p>
<p>Reuters Chicago Newsdesk - 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
